}","content":"

Segments use half-open time ranges `[start, end)` in seconds relative to the original input timeline. For example, `{"start": 610, "end": 613}` covers seconds 610, 611, and 612 with duration 3 seconds."},{"op":"replace","target":"| `threshold_ratio` | More aggressive | More conservative |","content":"| `threshold_ratio` | Stricter detection, fewer pauses flagged | More permissive/sensitive, more pauses flagged |"},{"op":"insert_after","target":"| `window_size` | Local context | Broader context |","content":"

Examples:
- `threshold_ratio=0.3`: only very quiet dips relative to nearby audio are detected
- `threshold_ratio=0.7`: moderate drops below the local average are also detected, producing more pause segments
- Smaller `window_size` reacts quickly to short-term volume changes; larger values smooth over longer sections and reduce sensitivity to brief dips
- `min_duration` is applied after consecutive low-energy seconds are grouped into segments, so increasing it removes short pauses even if they pass the threshold test"},{"op":"replace","target":"3. Mark seconds where energy < local_avg × threshold_ratio","content":"3. Mark seconds where `energy < local_avg × threshold_ratio`; increasing `threshold_ratio` causes more seconds to satisfy this condition"}]}

